 "drivers": "Wednesday's post-midterm relief rally (Dow +3.0%, S&P 500 +1.6%, the best day in about 18 months) is cooling: Dow futures are up about 0.7% but Nasdaq-100 futures are down about 0.75% as chips slide. Qualcomm is down about 11% pre-market after soft December-quarter profit guidance and a handset slump overshadowed a beat, and Arm is down about 7%; MU, AMD, SNDK, AVGO and the SOXX are 3–7% lower, after Korea's Kospi fell about 5% overnight (SK hynix about −9%). Earnings are driving big single-stock gaps: AppLovin, Unity, Warby Parker, Sunrun and Tapestry are up 16–23%, while Gildan, Snap, Dutch Bros and Fastly are down 11–23%. Overseas, the Hang Seng rose about 3.7% and the FTSE 100 hit its highest since August; the Bank of England was expected to raise rates 25 bp to 4% today. Oil has whipsawed after Wednesday's 8% plunge on US–Iran de-escalation hopes (WTI quoted from about $87 to $89 across sources this morning), gold is up about 1.4%, and Bitcoin is near $80K. Weekly jobless claims and Q3 productivity came out at 7:30 a.m. CT; results were not retrieved.",
